SUMMARY: Cinema Shift Festival
DESCRIPTION:Cinema Shift Festival is a one-night event that brings togeth
 er films and conversations about how AI is used in filmmaking.\n\nOn June
  5 at the Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema\, you’ll see a curated program of st
 ory-driven films where AI is part of the creative process - not the focus
 \, but the tool. The films are intimate\, funny\, and tense\, showing wha
 t this shift actually looks like on screen.\n\nAlongside the films\, shor
 t conversations explore how creators are working with AI today - from sto
 rytelling and editing to authorship and rights.\n\nThis event is for:\n\n
 – filmmakers\, directors\, and producers exploring new workflows\n\n– AI 
 creatives and technologists working with generative tools\n\n– VFX artist
 s\, editors\, and production professionals\n\n– agency creatives\, strate
 gists\, and brand teams\n\n– students and emerging creators in film and c
 reative technology\n\nIf you’re curious about where filmmaking is heading
  - and want to see it\, not just hear about it - this is a rare chance to
  experience it in a cinema setting.\n\nReserve your seat: https://luma.co
 m/CinemaShiftFestival2026 https://luma.com/CinemaShiftFestival2026
CATEGORIES:Film,Hot-Docs-Cinema
