DESCRIPTION:Kick off your weekend with a night of laughs at Collective Ar
 ts Toronto Friday\, June 5th.\n\n\nJoin us for a night of live comedy\, g
 reat drinks\, and good company in the heart of Toronto. Whether you're co
 ming out with friends\, planning a date night\, or just looking for somet
 hing fun to do on a Friday\, this is the perfect way to start the weekend
 .\n\n\nCome early\, grab a drink\, and settle in for an evening of live e
 ntertainment in a creative\, laid-back atmosphere. Our kitchen is open fr
 om 5pm\, serving up a great selection of authentic Mexican dishes.\n\n\nE
 vent Details:\n\nFriday\, June 5\, 2026\n\nCollective Arts Toronto (lower
  level venue)\n\n777 Dundas Street West\n\n19+ event\n\nDoors 7pm\n\nShow
  8pm\n\nTickets: $25 + taxes & fees (includes your first beverage)\n\n\nP
 resented by BHG Entertainment\n\n\n\nHeadliner\n\nCourtney Gilmour\n\nLet
  Me Hold You Baby (2022)\, Wonder Woman (2024)\n\n2x Juno Nominee (Best C
 omedy Album)\, Just for Laughs\, Trailer Park Boys\, Paw Patrol\n\n\nFeat
 uring\n\nTodd Graham\n\nBustin' Loose! (2019)\n\nJust for Laughs\, Roast 
 Battle Canada\n\n\nHosted by\n\nRob Bebenek\n\nEverything is Fine (2020)\
 n\nJust For Laughs\, Winnipeg Comedy Festival\n\n\nLocation\n\nCollective
  Arts Toronto\n\n\nlooking to book a show or special event at a collectiv
 e arts space?\n\nHit us up! Sen
