SUMMARY: Authors at Caversham: Rosemary Richings on thriving as a neurodi
 vergent person
DESCRIPTION:An afternoon of insights and practical information for neurod
 ivergent young people\, and anyone interested in better understanding and
  accommodating their needs\n\nRosemary Richings is a writer\, editor\, an
 d public speaker specializing in neurodiversity. She is the author of two
  books: Stumbling Through Space and Time: Living Life With Dyspraxia http
 s://www.cavershambooksellers.com/search/9781839972690?utm_source=luma \, 
 and the forthcoming Studying With Dyspraxia https://www.cavershambooksell
 ers.com/search/9781350524644?utm_source=luma . Her writing has been featu
 red in Travel + Leisure\, Broken Pencil Magazine\, Happiful Magazine\, an
 d numerous other websites.\n\nRosemary will give a presentation on naviga
 ting school and the workforce as a neurodivergent person.\n\nIn Stumbling
  Through Space and Time: Living Life With Dyspraxia https://www.caversham
 booksellers.com/search/9781839972690?utm_source=luma \, Rosemary shares h
 er experience of growing up dyspraxic\, and how it impacts her sense of s
 pace\, time and co-ordination. Diagnosed with DCD at the age of four\, Ro
 semary shares her insights and experience dealing with challenges\, from 
 coping with bullies in school to choosing a dyspraxia-friendly university
 \, pursuing self-employment and travelling abroad.\n\nIn Studying with Dy
 spraxia https://www.cavershambooksellers.com/search/9781350524644?utm_sou
 rce=luma \, Rosemary helps readers to understand what to expect at univer
 sity and gives support in adjusting to a more independent lifestyle. Cruc
 ially\, the book helps students to implement study strategies that really
  work.\n\nAccessibility Note: Rosemary will bring a small\, self-containe
 d sensory support table (quiet tools for regulation and focus). Attendees
  will be free to leave and come back\, or move around the room\, while th
 e event is in progress.
CATEGORIES:Book-Launch,Lecture/Book-Talk,Caversham-Booksellers
