  Friends / High Alpine Hut Network / Maris Pihlap / MMXKLS / Grdina/Lilli
 nger Duo / ADHD
DESCRIPTION:Wavelength @ St. Anne’s Block Party\n\nPresented with Sonic B
 oom\n\nCo-presented with Estonian Music Week and VEMU Estonian Museum Can
 ada\n\nFREE + ALL AGES\n\nDAY ONE\n\nMoneka Arabic Jazz (Toronto // Afric
 an grooves meet Arabic Folk)\n\nHigh Alpine Hut Network (Toronto // psych
 -jazz-rock fusion)\n\nMaris Pihlap (Tallinn // Estonian electronic ambien
 t pop)\n\nMMXKLS (Toronto + Haida Gwaii BC // grunge-folk ballads from Le
 mon Bucket Orkestra’s Mark Marczyk + Indigenous singer Kristi Lane Sincla
 ir)\n\nGrdina/Lillinger Duo (Vancouver + Berlin // Canadian/German jazz i
 mprov for Oud\, guitar + drums)\n\nADHD (Iceland // nature jazz-rock vibr
 ation quartet)\n\n+DJ Moussa\n\n\nDAY TWO\n\nLiving Hour (Winnipeg // dre
 amy noise-rock // Paper Bag Records\, en route to Wilco’s Solid Sound fes
 tival)\n\nTriples (Toronto // aka lo-fi indie-pop singer/songwriter Eva L
 ink)\n\nFleur Electra (Toronto-via-Saskatchewan // irresistibly catchy dr
 eam-pop)\n\nSunken Cages (New York // aka Ravish Momin\, Indian folk meet
 s electro-acoustic drums + loops)\n\nMother Of x Ensh (Toronto // industr
 ial synth beats)\n\nHouse of Whatever (neighbourhood DJ duo amps us up fo
 r Pride)\n\n\nWest-enders unite! While the world gathers in Toronto for t
 he FIFA World Cup\, come on down to Wavelength @ St. Anne’s for a good ol
 d-fashioned block party. Located in the parking lot off Gladstone Avenue\
 , this hidden oasis will be packed with live music\, food trucks\, art in
 stallations\, and local indie market vendors. FREE admission\, for All Ag
 es!\n\n\nNight One’s musical lineup features a transcendent line-up of ja
 zz and electronic grooves\, with a psychedelic touch. Night Two expands i
 nto dreamy territory\, bringing in experimental production and catchy mel
 odies. Artists will join us from across Canada and around the world\, to 
 form a globally-minded sound for this Father’s Day and pre-Pride weekend.
 \n\n\nFamilies are welcome and encouraged to join us in this summer kick-
 off with the community!\n\n\n#FWC26\, #WeAreToronto\n\nPoster by Leesa We
 stwood\n\nAccessibility:\n\nThe block party is located in the parking lot
  of St. Anne’s\, and is accessible from Gladstone Avenue. The lower lot i
 s wheelchair accessible\, and there is a slight ramp to go to the upper l
 ot.\n\n
CATEGORIES:Concert,Market,St.-Anne's-Parish-Hall,Art-Show/Gallery-Event,W
 avelength
