SUMMARY: The Improper Identity - written and directed by Miho Suzuki
DESCRIPTION:This show tells the story of immigrants’ journeys\, revealing
  the challenges\, resilience\, and lived realities of speaking English wi
 th a different accent. The show uses comical fantasy to metaphorically ex
 pose both speakers' and listeners' often unconscious stereotyping biases.
  And the show ultimately calls for a more mutually empathetic tomorrow.\n
 \nFollow Instagram (@theimproperidentity https://www.instagram.com/theimp
 roperidentity/ ) for BTS clips!\n\nPerformance schedule (Runtime - 55 min
 s):\n\n2nd July\, 9:45pm\n\n4th July\, 7:15pm\n\n5th July\, 4:00pm\n\n8th
  July\, 9:15pm\n\n9th July\, 4:30pm\n\n10th July\, 7:15pm\n\n11th July\, 
 9:30pm\n\n12th July\, 3:15pm\n\n\nTickets go on sale: June 3\n\nVisit The
  Improper Identity | Toronto Fringe Festival https://fringetoronto.com/fr
 inge/show/improper-identity for ticket prices and information.
CATEGORIES:Comedy,Dance---Performance---Theatre
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6a19fbc4ac49693c081d99e9/scaled_1024.jpg
