SUMMARY: 31st Annual Tim Hortons GWN Dragon Boat Challenge
DESCRIPTION:GWN Dragon Boat is proud to present the 31st Annual Tim Horto
 ns GWN Dragon Boat Challenge\, taking place on September 12 & 13\, 2026 a
 t Toronto’s scenic Marilyn Bell Park. This event proudly supports Tim Hor
 tons Foundation Camps.\n\nTwenty paddlers move in unison\, combining stre
 ngth and teamwork in a boat whose elaborate design originates from ancien
 t China. Social groups and businesses alike embrace the sport because it 
 builds camaraderie\, forms connections\, and promotes healthy lifestyles.
 \n\nAdmission to this family-friendly event is free\; races will begin at
  approximately 8:30am and will continue throughout each day. Festival gro
 unds will offer a variety of activities for all participants and spectato
 rs. Families can bring their children to enjoy live performances\, inflat
 able bounce houses/obstacle courses in the interactive Family Fun Zone. G
 rab a bite from one of our Food Trucks while wandering through the Health
  & Wellness Zone featuring exciting local products and services to assist
  in leading a healthy lifestyle. For all your shopping needs\, stop by th
 e Artisan Village and Vendor Marketplace. Last but definitely not least\,
  the Left Field Brewery Beer Garden will keep the party going located rig
 ht by the finish line with a live band performing on the main stage each 
 afternoon.\n\nNew teams and individuals are welcome! Invite friends\, fam
 ily\, colleagues - form a group of 16 to 25 people and sign-up a team tod
 ay. If you or a couple of friends are interested\, there is a pay per sea
 t option available\, contact us at info@gwndragonboat.com mailto:info@gwn
 dragonboat.com?subject=GWN%20Challenge%20-%20inquiry  to join.    \n\nGet
  in on the action – ask us how to get involved!\n\nFor more information\,
  visit https://gwndragonboat.com/festivals/tim-hortons-gwn-dragon-boat-ch
 allenge/ https://gwndragonboat.com/festivals/tim-hortons-gwn-dragon-boat-
 challenge/
CATEGORIES:Dragon-Boat,Water-Sports,Free-Admission
